+  - id: exp4208-verifier-as-detector-auroc
+    milestone: 2026.06.390
+    title: "PHASE A1 (HEADLINE-COMPLEMENTARY; cheap, cached) -- verifier-as-DETECTOR measurement. The 2026-06-14 P0 item 2: where SELECTION headroom is ~0, can the verifier still FLAG/REJECT a wrong output? Compute detection AUROC (verifier_score ranking is_correct) + precision@recall=0.9 + the accuracy-vs-coverage abstention curve across cached pools {Sudoku TRM snapshots, code HumanEval/MBPP, ARC GAP-4 pool, GSM8K}, and report it AGAINST each domain's SELECTION headroom (.387/.388). The headline is the DIVERGENCE: detection value where selection had none. Positive/negative controls (base rate + random-AUROC~0.5); sanity-check decoding before trusting any number; declare verifier_is_oracle per domain. NO new generation, NO training."
+    priority: high
+    track: verifier-oracle-distinct
+    max_turns: 60
+    agent_type: codex
+    model: gpt-5.5
+    inference_substrate: verifier_ensemble_against_cached_candidates
+    deliverable: results/experiment_4208_verifier_as_detector_auroc.json
+    prompt: |
+      CONTEXT: The 2026-06-14 P0 directive's COMPLEMENTARY axis. The SELECTOR metric (oracle@K - vote)
+      only measures "can the verifier pick a better answer from a pool." It does NOT measure detection:
+      can the verifier correctly FLAG/REJECT a wrong output (for abstention / "I don't know" /
+      filtering). Detection has value EVEN where selection headroom is ~0 (e.g. Sudoku-at-convergence:
+      no recoverable alternative to select, but the verifier can still tell you the answer is wrong).
+      This isolates that axis. It is CHEAP -- uses data we ALREADY have, no new generation/training.
+
+      EXISTING CODE TO READ FIRST:
+        - docs/research-notes/verifier-as-detector-measurement-spec.md (THE SPEC -- follow it)
+        - scripts/exp_verifier_detector_auroc.py (the probe -- extend/reuse, do NOT rewrite)
+        - results/arc3_trm_verifier_rerank.json (ARC GAP-4 pool), results/experiment_4175_headroom_gate_executable_census.json (cached code/math pools + per-domain SELECTION headroom)
+        - results/trm_runs/snapshots/ (Sudoku checkpoints) + nano-trm/src/nn/sudoku_evaluator.py (check_sudoku_validity)
+        - CLAUDE.md "Circularity / Oracle-Distinctness Discipline" + "Adversarial Artifact Verification" (FALSE_NEGATIVE_RISK, the degenerate-detector trap)
+
+      TASK: detection AUROC per domain vs SELECTION headroom; report the divergence; controls + decode sanity.
+
+      CONCRETE STEPS:
+        0. PRECONDITIONS (check BEFORE any compute): the cached pools above are loadable
+           (`ls results/arc3_trm_verifier_rerank.json results/experiment_4175_headroom_gate_executable_census.json`)
+           AND scripts/exp_verifier_detector_auroc.py imports. If any missing -> honest_verdict
+           `blocked_detector_cached_pools_missing` and STOP. NO LLM generation in this task.
+        1. For each domain load (output, is_correct) + compute the verifier_score per output (Sudoku:
+           satisfied_constraints/total via check_sudoku_validity -- FIRST sanity-check that greedy exact
+           reproduces ~0.79 test before trusting AUROC; code/math: the executable verifier; ARC: the
+           GAP-4 demo-fit score).
+        2. Compute detection_auroc (verifier_score vs is_correct) with bootstrap CI95, Brier,
+           precision@recall=0.9, and the accuracy-vs-coverage abstention curve. CONTROLS: report the
+           base rate (fraction correct) AND a random-score AUROC~0.5 baseline; AUROC must beat 0.5
+           CI95-excl to count. On Sudoku ALSO report AUROC restricted to VALID-BUT-WRONG outputs (the
+           hard detection case -- avoid over-claiming on the trivial invalid-grid split).
+        3. Report per-domain {detection_auroc, selector_headroom (from .387/.388), n, verifier_is_oracle}.
+           The headline is the DIVERGENCE: a high detection AUROC where selection headroom ~0.
