+  - id: exp4210-oracle-distinct-arc-verifier-beats-vote
+    milestone: 2026.06.390
+    title: "PHASE A3 (THE HEADLINE GATE, gated_on A2 selector_trained) -- does the ORACLE-DISTINCT learned ARC verifier BEAT majority vote OFF-ORACLE? On a HELD-OUT ARC candidate pool, rerank with the A2 learned verifier (verifier_is_oracle=false; does NOT execute the demos) vs majority-vote vs a MATCHED no-verifier control (same candidates/budget) vs oracle@K (the positive-control ceiling). The LOAD-BEARING gate: verifier@1 - vote@1, bootstrap CI95 EXCLUDES 0 AND headroom exists (oracle@K >> vote). Framed by ARBITER (arXiv:2605.26172) 'wrong-majority failures' -- the correct answer is in the pool but loses to a bigger wrong basin; the oracle-distinct verifier's job is to recover it. YES -> the first oracle-distinct verifier win (closes GAP-3-ties-vote; informs the DiffusionGemma gate). TIE-with-headroom -> honest null (GAP-3 frontier persists). No-headroom -> uninformative."
+    priority: high
+    track: verifier-oracle-distinct
+    max_turns: 70
+    agent_type: codex
+    model: gpt-5.5
+    operator_override: "2026-05-29 operator directive (standing) auto-override class 3 (versioned-lineage continuation): the oracle-distinct beats-vote measurement is MANDATED by the 2026-06-14 P0 directive (HEADLINE; verifier_is_oracle=false + MATCHED control + CI95-excl-0) -- false-positive scope-match vs retired GAP-3 rerank/selector exps; forward difference = a LEARNED oracle-distinct verifier (A2), not the execution oracle, with the matched-control de-confound the prior circular wins lacked."
+    inference_substrate: verifier_ensemble_against_cached_candidates
+    deliverable: results/experiment_4210_oracle_distinct_arc_verifier_beats_vote.json
+    gated_on:
+      - upstream: exp4209-oracle-distinct-arc-verifier-build
+        artifact_field: selector_trained
+        op: '=='
+        value: true
+    prompt: |
+      CONTEXT: THE .390 headline gate. A2 built an oracle-distinct learned ARC verifier (V-STaR-on-ARC,
+      verifier_is_oracle=false). Now measure whether it BEATS majority vote on a HELD-OUT ARC pool --
+      the deep, defensible claim the circular execution wins cannot make. ARBITER (arXiv:2605.26172)
+      names the headroom precisely: "wrong-majority failures" -- sampled trajectories cluster into
+      basins and vote picks the LARGEST basin, not the most accurate, so the correct answer is in the
+      pool but loses. A learned verifier that recovers those is the oracle-distinct win. The MATCHED
+      no-verifier control (same candidates, same budget) is the de-confound the prior circular wins
+      lacked.
+
+      EXISTING CODE TO READ FIRST:
+        - results/experiment_4209_oracle_distinct_arc_verifier_build.json (learned_verifier_path, oracle_distinct_auroc, verifier_is_oracle=false)
+        - results/arc3_trm_verifier_rerank.json (the ARC candidate pool; use a HELD-OUT split disjoint from A2's training folds)
+        - scripts/adversarial_verify.py (run it on the artifact -- check_circular_moat_overclaim), scripts/summarize_artifact.py
+        - research-references.md ".390 sweep" (ARBITER 2605.26172 wrong-majority basins; SCOPE 2512.15146 minority-recovery; ThinkPRM 2504.16828 learned-verifier-beats-vote precedent)
+        - CLAUDE.md "Circularity / Oracle-Distinctness Discipline" + "Adversarial Artifact Verification" (FALSE_NEGATIVE_RISK positive control)
+
+      TASK: held-out ARC rerank -- learned verifier vs vote vs matched control vs oracle@K; the decisive CI95 gate.
+
+      CONCRETE STEPS:
+        0. PRECONDITIONS: A2 reported selector_trained=true with a readable learned_verifier_path. If
+           missing/false -> honest_verdict `complete_oracle_distinct_arc_gate_deferred_no_built_verifier`
+           and STOP.
+        1. On a HELD-OUT ARC split (disjoint from A2 folds, N as large as the pool allows; if N<30 note
+           the CLT-floor caveat), compute per-task: vote@1 (majority candidate), verifier@1 (candidate
+           maximizing the A2 LEARNED score -- NO demo execution at inference), oracle@K (any candidate
+           exactly correct = the POSITIVE CONTROL), and a MATCHED no-verifier control (same candidate
+           budget, random/first selection) so the comparison is budget-equal (arXiv:2511.02886).
+        2. POSITIVE CONTROL FIRST: if oracle@K ~= vote@1 (no recoverable headroom) the corpus is
+           ceiling-saturated -> the null is UNINFORMATIVE (FALSE_NEGATIVE_RISK) -> report
+           `complete_oracle_distinct_arc_no_headroom_uninformative`, do NOT claim the verifier fails.
+        3. THE GATE: verifier_minus_vote = verifier@1 - vote@1, task-level bootstrap CI95 (>=2000
+           resamples). Emit oracle_distinct_beats_vote BARE bool := (CI95 excludes 0 AND delta>0 AND
+           headroom exists). Run adversarial_verify.py (it must NOT raise CIRCULAR_MOAT_OVERCLAIM since
+           verifier_is_oracle=false). Honest headline: one of {oracle_distinct_verifier_beats_vote,
+           oracle_distinct_verifier_ties_vote_with_headroom, oracle_distinct_arc_no_headroom_uninformative}.
+      REQUIRED ARTIFACT FIELDS:
+        honest_verdict:
+          principle: "Terminal-prefixed. A clean beats-vote win, a clean ties-vote-with-headroom null, and an honest no-headroom-uninformative are ALL COMPLETE, decision-grade -- the first clean read on the oracle-distinct frontier either way."
+        oracle_distinct_beats_vote:
+          principle: "BARE bool: verifier@1 - vote@1 CI95 excludes 0 AND delta>0 AND headroom exists -- the de-confounded oracle-distinct win (the GAP-3-ties-vote gap closed); NOT a circular execution result."
+        verifier_minus_vote_delta:
+          principle: "verifier@1 - vote@1 on held-out ARC -- the oracle-distinct lift; recovers the wrong-majority-failure answers (ARBITER) a flat vote discards."
+        verifier_minus_vote_ci95:
+          principle: "Task-level bootstrap CI95 of the delta -- excluding 0 is what distinguishes a real oracle-distinct win from noise."
+        oracle_at_k:
+          principle: "The positive-control ceiling (any candidate exactly correct) -- if oracle@K ~= vote the null is uninformative (FALSE_NEGATIVE_RISK), not a verifier failure."
+        matched_control_delta:
+          principle: "verifier@1 minus the budget-matched no-verifier control -- isolates the verifier's contribution from the candidate budget (arXiv:2511.02886)."
+        verifier_is_oracle:
+          principle: "BARE bool=false -- this measurement uses the LEARNED verifier (no demo execution); only this makes the result headline/gate-eligible (Circularity Discipline; adversarial_verify CIRCULAR_MOAT_OVERCLAIM must stay clean)."
+        random_seed:
+          principle: "Determinism precondition; the held-out split + bootstrap must be reproducible."
+        reproducibility_checksum:
+          principle: "Hash of the held-out pool + the learned verifier; lets a third party re-run the decisive gate."
+      ACCEPTANCE GATE:
+        - condition: "oracle_at_k reported (positive control) AND verifier_minus_vote_delta + verifier_minus_vote_ci95 + matched_control_delta reported with verifier_is_oracle=false, OR an honest no-headroom/deferred verdict"
+          principle: "Decisive only with the positive control (real headroom) + the matched control + the oracle-distinct (non-circular) verifier; otherwise honestly defer rather than emit an uninformative or circular result."
+
+      Run: `python3 {project_root}/results/experiment_4210_oracle_distinct_arc_verifier_beats_vote.py`
